IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wica-tables`
IMPORT `wica-compensation`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 -- worked cases for s 7 and the First
-- Schedule.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `in course` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `contrary evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `drink or drugs` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `self injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Accident
DECIDE `an accident` `in course` `contrary evidence` `drink or drugs` `self injury` IS
    Accident WITH
        `personal injury was caused to an employee by an accident` IS TRUE
        `the accident arose in the course of the employment` IS `in course`
        `there is evidence that it did not arise out of the employment` IS `contrary evidence`
        `the injury is directly attributable to the employee being under the influence of alcohol or a drug at the time` IS `drink or drugs`
        `deliberate self-injury or deliberate aggravation of an accidental injury by the employee` IS `self injury`
        `the injury was suffered in a fight or an assault` IS FALSE
        `the employee did not assault anyone, or did so in private defence under Penal Code sections 97 to 106A` IS FALSE
        `the employee was breaking up or preventing the fight or assault` IS FALSE
        `the employee was safeguarding life or property or maintaining law and order` IS FALSE

`an ordinary workplace accident` MEANS `an accident` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `7 -- liability, and the section 7(4) presumption`

#ASSERT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` `an ordinary workplace accident`
#ASSERT NOT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an accident` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 7(4) is rebuttable, and this is the rebuttal doing its work.
#ASSERT `the accident is taken to arise out of the employment` `an ordinary workplace accident`
#ASSERT NOT `the accident is taken to arise out of the employment` (`an accident` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an accident` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT NOT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an accident` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an accident` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§ `7(2)(c) -- the fight exclusion and its exceptions`

GIVEN `assaulted nobody or private defence` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `breaking up` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `safeguarding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Accident
DECIDE `an injury in a fight where the employee` `assaulted nobody or private defence` `breaking up` `safeguarding` IS
    Accident WITH
        `personal injury was caused to an employee by an accident` IS TRUE
        `the accident arose in the course of the employment` IS TRUE
        `there is evidence that it did not arise out of the employment` IS FALSE
        `the injury is directly attributable to the employee being under the influence of alcohol or a drug at the time` IS FALSE
        `deliberate self-injury or deliberate aggravation of an accidental injury by the employee` IS FALSE
        `the injury was suffered in a fight or an assault` IS TRUE
        `the employee did not assault anyone, or did so in private defence under Penal Code sections 97 to 106A` IS `assaulted nobody or private defence`
        `the employee was breaking up or preventing the fight or assault` IS `breaking up`
        `the employee was safeguarding life or property or maintaining law and order` IS `safeguarding`

#ASSERT `the fight exclusion in section 7(2)(c) applies` (`an injury in a fight where the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an injury in a fight where the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an injury in a fight where the employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an injury in a fight where the employee` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the employer is liable to pay compensation` (`an injury in a fight where the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§ `The First Schedule tables, recovered from the PDF`

-- The two checks that were run on the recovered tables, repeated here so that a
-- future change to the generator cannot pass silently.
--
-- Endpoints and a sample of each table.
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 14 EQUALS 136
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 10 EQUALS 136
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 32 EQUALS 121
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 40 EQUALS 108
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 65 EQUALS 53
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 66 EQUALS 48
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 80 EQUALS 48

#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 14 EQUALS 181
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 32 EQUALS 160
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 40 EQUALS 144
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 65 EQUALS 77
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 66 EQUALS 72
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 80 EQUALS 72

-- ROW 32 IS THE ONE THE OLD DEPOSIT LOST. In WICA2019.txt it is blank and 33
-- carries 121. The recovered table puts 121 against 32 and 120 against 33, and
-- the sequence 122, 121, 120 across ages 31 to 33 is monotonic as it must be.
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 31 EQUALS 122
#ASSERT `the Table A factor` 33 EQUALS 120

-- Table B is higher than Table A at every age: the Act values a surviving
-- incapacitated employee above a death.
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 14 GREATER THAN `the Table A factor` 14
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 40 GREATER THAN `the Table A factor` 40
#ASSERT `the Table B factor` 66 GREATER THAN `the Table A factor` 66

§ `First Schedule paragraph 1 -- death`

GIVEN `ame` IS A NUMBER, `age` IS A NUMBER, `on or after` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Injury
DECIDE `an injury with` `ame` `age` `on or after` IS
    Injury WITH
        `the average monthly earnings` IS `ame`
        `the age on the next birthday at the time of the accident` IS `age`
        `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` IS `on or after`
        `the percentage of loss of earning capacity` IS 1

-- A 39-year-old (age 40 on the next birthday) on $3,000 AME: 3000 x 108 is
-- 324,000, above the post-2025 cap, so the cap governs.
#ASSERT `the unadjusted death compensation` (`an injury with` 3000 40 TRUE) EQUALS 324000
#ASSERT `the compensation for death` (`an injury with` 3000 40 TRUE) EQUALS 269000
-- The same accident a day earlier: the older, lower cap.
#ASSERT `the compensation for death` (`an injury with` 3000 40 FALSE) EQUALS 225000

-- A low earner: $400 x 108 is 43,200, below the floor.
#ASSERT `the unadjusted death compensation` (`an injury with` 400 40 TRUE) EQUALS 43200
#ASSERT `the compensation for death` (`an injury with` 400 40 TRUE) EQUALS 91000
#ASSERT `the compensation for death` (`an injury with` 400 40 FALSE) EQUALS 76000

-- Between the floor and the cap, the product governs untouched.
#ASSERT `the compensation for death` (`an injury with` 1500 40 TRUE) EQUALS 162000

-- THE AGE NOW MATTERS, which it could not before the tables were recovered.
-- The same earnings at 66 instead of 40: 1500 x 48 is 72,000, below the floor,
-- so an older worker's family is held up to the floor while a younger worker's
-- is paid on the product.
#ASSERT `the unadjusted death compensation` (`an injury with` 1500 66 TRUE) EQUALS 72000
#ASSERT `the compensation for death` (`an injury with` 1500 66 TRUE) EQUALS 91000

-- The clamp itself, at its exact boundaries. "less than" and "more than", so
-- the floor and the cap are each inside the permitted range.
#ASSERT `the amount held between the floor and the cap` 91000 91000 269000 EQUALS 91000
#ASSERT `the amount held between the floor and the cap` 90999 91000 269000 EQUALS 91000
#ASSERT `the amount held between the floor and the cap` 269000 91000 269000 EQUALS 269000
#ASSERT `the amount held between the floor and the cap` 269001 91000 269000 EQUALS 269000
#ASSERT `the amount held between the floor and the cap` 150000 91000 269000 EQUALS 150000

§ `First Schedule paragraph 2 -- total incapacity, and the order of operations`

-- THE ORDER MATTERS. The floor and cap bite on C, and C + 0.25C is applied
-- afterwards, so the final sum exceeds the stated cap by a quarter.
-- $5,000 AME at age 40: 5000 x 144 = 720,000, clamped to 346,000.
#ASSERT `C` (`an injury with` 5000 40 TRUE) EQUALS 346000
#ASSERT `the compensation for total incapacity` (`an injury with` 5000 40 TRUE) EQUALS 432500

-- Likewise at the floor: a clamped C of 116,000 pays out 145,000.
#ASSERT `C` (`an injury with` 100 40 TRUE) EQUALS 116000
#ASSERT `the compensation for total incapacity` (`an injury with` 100 40 TRUE) EQUALS 145000

-- Before 1 November 2025, the older figures.
#ASSERT `C` (`an injury with` 5000 40 FALSE) EQUALS 289000
#ASSERT `the compensation for total incapacity` (`an injury with` 5000 40 FALSE) EQUALS 361250

-- Unclamped, the uplift is plain: $1,000 AME at age 40 is 144,000, inside the
-- band, and the payout is a quarter more.
#ASSERT `C` (`an injury with` 1000 40 TRUE) EQUALS 144000
#ASSERT `the compensation for total incapacity` (`an injury with` 1000 40 TRUE) EQUALS 180000

§ `First Schedule paragraph 3 -- partial incapacity`

GIVEN `ame` IS A NUMBER, `age` IS A NUMBER, `pct` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Injury
DECIDE `a partial injury with` `ame` `age` `pct` IS
    Injury WITH
        `the average monthly earnings` IS `ame`
        `the age on the next birthday at the time of the accident` IS `age`
        `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` IS TRUE
        `the percentage of loss of earning capacity` IS `pct`

-- Paragraph 3 multiplies C, not the paragraph 2 figure.
#ASSERT `the compensation for partial incapacity` (`a partial injury with` 1000 40 0.5) EQUALS 72000

-- AT 100% LOSS OF EARNING CAPACITY the partial and total figures still differ,
-- by exactly the quarter that paragraph 2 adds and paragraph 3 does not.
#ASSERT `the compensation for partial incapacity` (`a partial injury with` 1000 40 1) EQUALS 144000
#ASSERT `the compensation for total incapacity` (`a partial injury with` 1000 40 1) EQUALS 180000
